  "metadata_synthesis": "1998 Japanese drama film. Directed by Hirokazu Koreeda. Documentary-style interviews. Blends fantasy with existential introspection.",
  "setting_and_subculture": "A bureaucratic afterlife. A gentle limbo waiting room. A makeshift film studio for recreating memories. Quiet, peaceful transition spaces.",
  "visual_tone_and_feel": "Cinematic. Gentle. Sweet. Strangely peaceful. Earthy and grounded. The raw aesthetic of an indie documentary.",
  "media_era_tone": "Late 90s international cinema. Deeply contemplative. A quiet, poetic love letter to the art of filmmaking.",
  "pacing_and_structure": "Gentle and measured. Paced like a calm breath. Individual camera-facing interviews. A slow, methodical search for a single defining moment.",
  "atmosphere_and_mood": "Warm nostalgia. Introspective. Melancholy but sweet. Strangely peaceful. A quiet ache of profound realization.",
  "themes_and_messages": "Distilling life into a single moment. Being part of someone else's chosen memory. The weight of eternity. Cinema as the ultimate act of remembering.",
  "character_relationships": "Quietly vulnerable. Guides interviewing the recently departed. Souls discovering their unexpected impact on others. A shared, tender mortality.",
  "lead_character_type": "The recently deceased. Reflective, searching souls. Happy-go-lucky individuals forced to look back. Afterlife bureaucrats functioning as film crews.",
  "story_and_plot_type": "Existential drama. Magical realism. A bureaucratic procedural about selecting one perfect memory for eternity.",
  "who_and_when": "Everyday people at the end of their lives. A timeless, gentle bureaucracy. Late 20th-century souls reflecting on existence.",
  "emotional_evocation": "A ripple of introspection. Quiet devastation. Heartwarming discovery. The ultimate compliment of being someone's greatest happiness."
